('399b3289-93ad-58d5-8b72-87c6cc677ca5', '50ff4bc9-26e6-445a-abf4-2137ff76c6eb', 'c32a7123-0b11-417e-a3dd-2024f9fdf5d2', 'a-level', 'P2.1', '9702 coursebook P2.1 · Planning and analysis', 25, 25, 'It is suggested that the resistance R of a wire of fixed length is related to its diameter d by R = k/d². Which graph and result would support this?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'A graph of R against 1/d² is a straight line through the origin', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'R ∝ 1/d² means R against 1/d² is a line through the origin (or lg R against lg d has gradient −2). Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: plot R against 1/d². C1: straight line through origin. A1: B (A graph of R against 1/d² is a straight line through the origin).', 3, NULL, NULL),
