or">0.4</text><line x1="35.8" y1="63.7" x2="39.8" y2="63.7" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="32.8" y="63.7" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0.6</text><line x1="35.8" y1="34" x2="39.8" y2="34" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="32.8" y="34" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0.8</text><text x="210.9" y="274" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">lg (r / m)</text><text x="35.8" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">lg (F / N)</text><polyline points="39.8,48.9 382,236.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="47.8" y="40.9" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0.70</text></svg>', 'A straight line on a graph of lg F against lg r, meeting the lg F axis at 0.70 and falling with gradient −2.1.'),
('40a9f94f-a554-5168-a0ab-374e29abba04', '50ff4bc9-26e6-445a-abf4-2137ff76c6eb', 'c32a7123-0b11-417e-a3dd-2024f9fdf5d2', 'a-level', 'P2.1', '9702 coursebook P2.1 · Planning and analysis', 27, 27, 'A student plans to find how the frequency of the fundamental of a stretched wire depends on its tension. Which quantities must be kept constant?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The vibrating length and the type and diameter of the wire', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'f depends on length, tension and mass per unit length; only the tension is varied. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: length. C1: wire (mass per unit length). A1: C (The vibrating length and the type and diameter of the wire).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('124a79fc-d907-59aa-b2e8-436d3e7d982a', '50ff4bc9-26e6-445a-abf4-2137ff76c6eb', 'c32a7123-0b11-417e-a3dd-2024f9fdf5d2', 'a-level', 'P2.1', '9702 coursebook P2.1 · Planning and analysis', 28, 28, 'The relationship T = 2π√(m/k) for a mass on a spring is tested by plotting T² against m. The gradient is 0.16 s² kg⁻¹. Calculate the spring constant k.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '246.7', 'N m⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'T² = (4π²/k)m, so k = 4π² ÷ 0.16 = 247 N m⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: gradient = 4π²/k. C1: rearranged. A1: k = 247 N m⁻¹.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg7421c696-t fg7421c696-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg7421c696-t">T² against m</title><desc id="fg7421c696-d">A straight line through the origin on a graph of T² against m, with gradient 0.16 s² kg⁻¹.</desc><line x1="39.8" y1="34" x2="39.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="108.2" y1="34" x2="108.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="176.7" y1="34" x2="176.7" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="245.1" y1="34" x2="245.1" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="313.6" y1="34" x2="313.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="39.8" y1="242" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fi