ill:currentColor">0.20</text><text x="210.9" y="274" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">m / kg</text><text x="35.8" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">T² / s²</text><polyline points="39.8,242 382,75.6" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'A straight line through the origin on a graph of T² against m, with gradient 0.16 s² kg⁻¹.'),
('ab257fa3-8714-5b9e-895f-86cec3b32567', '50ff4bc9-26e6-445a-abf4-2137ff76c6eb', 'c32a7123-0b11-417e-a3dd-2024f9fdf5d2', 'a-level', 'P2.1', '9702 coursebook P2.1 · Planning and analysis', 29, 29, 'A quantity follows y = ae^(bx). A graph of ln y against x has gradient 0.35 and intercept 1.20 on the ln y axis. Calculate y when x = 4.0.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '13.46', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'ln y = 1.20 + 0.35 × 4.0 = 2.60, so y = e^(2.60) = 13.5. Mark scheme (4 marks). M1: ln y = ln a + bx. C1: ln y = 2.60. C1: exponentiate. A1: y = 13.5.', 4, NULL, NULL),
('aab9b47c-f255-5acb-a8ad-5dbaf9beff05', '50ff4bc9-26e6-445a-abf4-2137ff76c6eb', 'c32a7123-0b11-417e-a3dd-2024f9fdf5d2', 'a-level', 'P2.1', '9702 coursebook P2.1 · Planning and analysis', 30, 30, 'A student thinks the time t for a ball to roll down a slope of angle θ obeys t = k/√(sin θ). What should be plotted to test this?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 't against 1/√(sin θ), expecting a straight line through the origin', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Plotting t against 1/√(sin θ) linearises the expected relationship. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: correct axes. C1: line through origin. A1: A (t against 1/√(sin θ), expecting a straight line through the origin).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('836836d7-81f8-57d9-8152-c99e038f3448', '50ff4bc9-26e6-445a-abf4-2137ff76c6eb', 'c32a7123-0b11-417e-a3dd-2024f9fdf5d2', 'a-level', 'P2.1', '9702 coursebook P2.1 · Planning and analysis', 31, 31, 'Using s = ½at², a student plots s against t² for a trolley released from rest. The gradient is 0.42 m s⁻². Calculate the acceleration a.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.84', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Gradient = a/2, so a = 2 × 0.42 = 0.84 m s⁻². Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: gradient = ½a. C1: value. A1: a = 0.84 m s⁻².', 3, NULL, NULL),
('525c92b5-1be7-5b9a-a76a-3e6568430685', '50ff4bc9-26e6-445a-abf4-2137ff76c6eb', 'c32a7123-0b11-417e-a3dd-2024f9fdf5d2', 'a-level', 'P2.1', '9702 coursebook P2.1 · Planning and analysis', 32, 32, 'The best-fit line on a graph of lg y against lg x passes through (0.20, 1.10) and (0.80, 2.30). If y = kxⁿ, find n.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'n = gradient = (2.30 − 1.10) ÷ (0.80 − 0.20) = 2.0. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: gradient = n. C1: values from two points. A1: n = 2.0.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg5867ddb1-t fg5867ddb1-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg5867ddb1-t">Log–log best-fit line</title><desc id="fg5867ddb1-d">A best-fit line on a graph of lg y against lg x through the points (0.20, 1.10) and (0.80, 2.30).</desc><line x1="24" y1="34" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="95.6" y1="34" x2="95.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="167.2" y1="34" x2="167.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="238.8" y1="34" x2="238.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="310.4" y1="34" x2="310.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:roun