('4909b3c6-e080-5bf9-b3d8-c653523b1cca', '50ff4bc9-26e6-445a-abf4-2137ff76c6eb', 'c32a7123-0b11-417e-a3dd-2024f9fdf5d2', 'a-level', 'P2.1', '9702 coursebook P2.1 · Planning and analysis', 34, 34, 'Why should a plan include a short trial (preliminary) experiment?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'To choose suitable ranges, apparatus and values before the main readings are taken', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'A trial run shows which values are practical and measurable. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: choose range. C1: check apparatus works. A1: D (To choose suitable ranges, apparatus and values before the main readings are taken).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('a86cc17a-8482-5390-97fd-a5f833d56f29', '50ff4bc9-26e6-445a-abf4-2137ff76c6eb', 'c32a7123-0b11-417e-a3dd-2024f9fdf5d2', 'a-level', 'P2.1', '9702 coursebook P2.1 · Planning and analysis', 35, 35, 'An experiment uses a sealed γ-ray source. Which set of precautions is appropriate?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Handle it with long tongs, keep it at a distance and minimise the time it is out of its lead box', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Distance, time and shielding reduce the dose. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: tongs/distance. C1: minimise time, store shielded. A1: B (Handle it with long tongs, keep it at a distance and minimise the time it is out of its lead box).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('ce2696f1-64c8-5deb-939f-19d7b88cf133', '50ff4bc9-26e6-445a-abf4-2137ff76c6eb', 'c32a7123-0b11-417e-a3dd-2024f9fdf5d2', 'a-level', 'P2.1', '9702 coursebook P2.1 · Planning and analysis', 36, 36, 'The count rate C through an absorber of thickness x follows C = C₀e^(−µx). A graph of ln C against x has gradient −0.12 mm⁻¹. Calculate the thickness that halves the count rate, in mm.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '5.776 mm', 'mm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'µ = 0.12 mm⁻¹; x½ = ln 2 ÷ 0.12 = 5.78 mm. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: µ = −gradient. C1: x½ = ln 2/µ. A1: x½ = 5.78 mm.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('61e4e478-9513-5a2a-b24a-1bad7958f95e', '50ff4bc9-26e6-445a-abf4-2137ff76c6eb', 'c32a7123-0b11-417e-a3dd-2024f9fdf5d2', 'a-level', 'P2.1', '9702 coursebook P2.1 · Planning and analysis', 37, 37, 'How can a student decide whether data fit y = kxⁿ rather than y = kx + c?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Plot lg y against lg x: a power law gives a straight line whose gradient is n', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Only a power law gives a straight log–log graph. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: log–log graph. C1: straight line test. A1: C (Plot lg y against lg x: a power law gives a straight line whose gradient is n).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('4512caf2-58f5-54d3-8574-668ff6a54dd0', '50ff4bc9-26e6-445a-abf4-2137ff76c6eb', 'c32a7123-0b11-417e-a3dd-2024f9fdf5d2', 'a-level', 'P2.1', '9702 coursebook P2.1 · Planning and analysis', 38, 38, 'A power law y = kxⁿ has n = 0.50 according to a log–log graph, and y = 6.0 when x = 4.0. Calculate k.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '3', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'k = y ÷ xⁿ = 6.0 ÷ 4.0^0.50 = 3.0. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: k = y/xⁿ. C1: substitution. A1: k = 3.0.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('546b19f6-aaa4-511c-8525-7596a9eb14b6', '50ff4bc9-26e6-445a-abf4-2137ff76c6eb', 'c32a7123-0b11-417e-a3dd-2024f9fdf5d2', 'a-level', 'P2.1', '9702 coursebook P2.1 · Planning and analysis', 39, 39, 'A plan is to measure the resistance of a wire as its length is varied. Why should the current be kept small and switched off between readings?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'So that the wire does not heat up, because its resistance changes with temperature', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Temperature is a control variable that the current could change. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: heating effect. C1: R depends on temperature. C1: temperature controlled. A1: A (So that the wire does not heat up, because its resistance changes with temperature).', 4, NULL, NULL),
('9637be23-d609-587d-89de-bf2460abf6f8', '50ff4bc9-26e6-445a-abf4-2137ff76c6eb', 'c32a7123-0b11-417e-a3dd-2024f9fdf5d2', 'a-level', 'P2.1', '9702 coursebook P2.1 · Planning and analysis', 40, 40, 'A student times the fall of a ball through a fixed height for different heights h and plots t² against h. The gradient is 0.204 s² m⁻¹. Calculate g.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '9.804', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'h = ½gt², so t² = (2/g)h and g = 2 ÷ 0.204 = 9.80 m s⁻². Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: gradient = 2/g. C1: rearranged. A1: g = 9.80 m s⁻².', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg0d1e9550-t fg0d1e9550-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg0d1e9550-t">t² against h</title><desc id="fg0d1e9550-d">A straight line through the origin on a graph of t² against fall height h, gradient 0.204 s² m⁻¹.</desc><line x1="39.8" y1="34" x2="39.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="108.2" y1="34" x2="108.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="176.7" y1="34" x2="176.7" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="245.1" y1="34" x2="245.1" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="313.6" y1="34" x2="313.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="39.8" y1="242" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);strok