('92166e18-bf2b-5ff1-857b-bd2fd1331a09', '50ff4bc9-26e6-445a-abf4-2137ff76c6eb', 'c32a7123-0b11-417e-a3dd-2024f9fdf5d2', 'a-level', 'P2.1', '9702 coursebook P2.1 · Planning and analysis', 42, 42, 'A pendulum obeys T = 2π√(L/g). A student plots T² against L and finds a gradient of 4.05 s² m⁻¹. (a) Show that the gradient equals 4π²/g. (b) Calculate g.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '9.748', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) T² = 4π²L/g, a straight line through the origin of gradient 4π²/g. (b) g = 4π² ÷ 4.05 = 9.75 m s⁻². Mark scheme (6 marks). B1: square both sides. B1: compare with y = mx. M1: g = 4π²/gradient. C1: substitution. C1: value. A1: g = 9.75 m s⁻².', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg09e4fd1f-t fg09e4fd1f-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg09e4fd1f-t">T² against L</title><desc id="fg09e4fd1f-d">A straight line through the origin on a graph of T² against pendulum length L, gradient 4.05 s² m⁻¹.</desc><line x1="24" y1="34" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="95.6" y1="34" x2="95.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="167.2" y1="34" x2="167.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="238.8" y1="34" x2="238.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="310.4" y1="34" x2="310.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:rou