('02fdc76f-cbce-53e2-a083-d263585c77ce', '50ff4bc9-26e6-445a-abf4-2137ff76c6eb', 'c32a7123-0b11-417e-a3dd-2024f9fdf5d2', 'a-level', 'P2.1', '9702 coursebook P2.1 · Planning and analysis', 43, 43, 'The amplitude A of a damped oscillation follows A = A₀e^(−t/τ). A graph of ln(A/mm) against t/s passes through (0, 2.30) and (20, 1.50). (a) State what the gradient represents. (b) Calculate τ.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '25', 's', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) ln A = ln A₀ − t/τ, so the gradient is −1/τ. (b) Gradient = (1.50 − 2.30) ÷ (20 − 0) = −0.040 s⁻¹, so τ = 1 ÷ 0.040 = 25.0 s. Mark scheme (5 marks). B1: gradient = −1/τ. C1: gradient value. M1: τ = −1/gradient. C1: value. A1: τ = 25.0 s.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg27163080-t fg27163080-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg27163080-t">ln A against t</title><desc id="fg27163080-d">A straight line on a graph of ln A against t through (0, 2.30) and (20, 1.50).</desc><line x1="33" y1="34" x2="33" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="120.3" y1="34" x2="120.3" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="207.5" y1="34" x2="207.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="294.8" y1="34" x2="294.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="33" y1="242" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linec