('58fa2971-2418-5ae7-928f-edfd99c195ea', '50ff4bc9-26e6-445a-abf4-2137ff76c6eb', 'c32a7123-0b11-417e-a3dd-2024f9fdf5d2', 'a-level', 'P2.1', '9702 coursebook P2.1 · Planning and analysis', 47, 47, 'A graph of lg y against lg x is a straight line through (0.40, 1.62) and (1.20, 0.82). For y = kxⁿ: (a) find n; (b) find k; (c) find y when x = 5.0. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '20.94', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) n = (0.82 − 1.62) ÷ (1.20 − 0.40) = −1.0. (b) lg k = 1.62 + 1.0 × 0.40 = 2.02, k = 10^2.02 = 104.7. (c) y = 104.7 × 5.0^(−1.0) = 20.9. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: n. M1: lg k from a point. C1: k. M1: y = kxⁿ. C1: value. A1: y = 20.9.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg771bed8b-t fg771bed8b-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg771bed8b-t">Falling log–log line</title><desc id="fg771bed8b-d">A straight line on a graph of lg y against lg x through (0.40, 1.62) and (1.20, 0.82).</desc><line x1="33" y1="34" x2="33" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="82.9" y1="34" x2="82.9" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="132.7" y1="34" x2="132.7" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="182.6" y1="34" x2="182.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="232.4" y1="34" x2="232.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="282.3" y1="34" x2="282.3" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-li