('941cecf8-c336-533d-9ff2-3a32457bd02a', '50ff4bc9-26e6-445a-abf4-2137ff76c6eb', 'c32a7123-0b11-417e-a3dd-2024f9fdf5d2', 'a-level', 'P2.1', '9702 coursebook P2.1 · Planning and analysis', 48, 48, 'For a filament lamp, I = kVⁿ. A graph of lg(I/A) against lg(V/V) has gradient 0.60 and intercept −1.40. (a) Find k. (b) Calculate the current at 6.0 V, in mA.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '116.7 mA', 'mA', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) k = 10^(−1.40) = 0.03981. (b) I = 0.03981 × 6.0^0.60 = 0.1167 A. In mA: 0.1167 × 10³ = 117. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: k from intercept. M1: I = kVⁿ. C1: substitution. C1: mA. A1: I = 117 mA.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg00bdbb5b-t fg00bdbb5b-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg00bdbb5b-t">Log–log graph for a filament lamp</title><desc id="fg00bdbb5b-d">A straight line on a graph of lg I against lg V for a filament lamp, gradient 0.60, meeting the lg I axis at −1.40.</desc><line x1="39.8" y1="34" x2="39.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="96.8" y1="34" x2="96.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="153.8" y1="34" x2="153.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="210.9" y1="34" x2="210.9" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="267.9" y1="34" x2="267.9" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="325" y1="34" x2="325" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;str