('2164db24-dcec-5673-9581-825a3ce6e029', '50ff4bc9-26e6-445a-abf4-2137ff76c6eb', 'ce473f5f-8864-4efe-be59-be54ed9c0caa', 'a-level', 'P2.3', '9702 coursebook P2.3 · Analysis of the data', 41, 41, 'For a cell, 1/I = R/E + r/E. A graph of 1/I against R has gradient 0.125 A⁻¹ Ω⁻¹ and intercept 0.25 A⁻¹. Calculate r.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2', 'Ω', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'E = 1 ÷ 0.125 = 8.0 V; r = intercept × E = 0.25 × 8.0 = 2.0 Ω. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: E = 1/gradient. C1: r = intercept × E. A1: r = 2.0 Ω.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg5c966059-t fg5c966059-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg5c966059-t">1/I against R</title><desc id="fg5c966059-d">A straight line on a graph of 1/I against R, intercept 0.25 A⁻¹ on the 1/I axis and gradient 0.125 A⁻¹ Ω⁻¹.</desc><line x1="33" y1="34" x2="33" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="102.8" y1="34" x2="102.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="172.6" y1="34" x2="172.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="242.4" y1="34" x2="242.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="312.2" y1="34" x2="312.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="33" y1="242" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;strok