('062ec32e-64c4-53d8-ba48-45691d5144aa', '50ff4bc9-26e6-445a-abf4-2137ff76c6eb', 'ce473f5f-8864-4efe-be59-be54ed9c0caa', 'a-level', 'P2.3', '9702 coursebook P2.3 · Analysis of the data', 45, 45, 'Readings x = 2.0, 3.0, 5.0, 8.0 and y = 11.3, 20.8, 44.7, 90.5 are thought to obey y = kxⁿ. (a) Use the first and last readings to find n. (b) Find k. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '3.993', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) n = (lg 90.5 − lg 11.3) ÷ (lg 8.0 − lg 2.0) = 1.501. (b) k = 11.3 ÷ 2.0^1.501 = 3.99. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: logs of data. M1: gradient of log–log. C1: n. M1: k = y/xⁿ. C1: value. A1: k = 3.99.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 410" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg0490afea-t fg0490afea-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg0490afea-t">Readings of y against x</title><desc id="fg0490afea-d">Table and graph of y against x: (2.0, 11.3), (3.0, 20.8), (5.0, 44.7), (8.0, 90.5), on a curve bending upwards.</desc><g transform="translate(0,0)"><rect x="152.2" y="8" width="95.6" height="140" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="152.2" y="8" width="95.6" height="28" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="174.1" y="22" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">x</text><text x="221.9" y="22" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">y</text><line x1="196.1" y1="8" x2="196.1" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="152.2" y1="36" x2="247.8" y2="36" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-l