('3668eb64-971c-59f8-934e-9a00bce84e5a', '50ff4bc9-26e6-445a-abf4-2137ff76c6eb', 'ce473f5f-8864-4efe-be59-be54ed9c0caa', 'a-level', 'P2.3', '9702 coursebook P2.3 · Analysis of the data', 46, 46, 'A count rate (corrected for background) is 640, 452, 320, 226 and 160 counts per minute at t = 0, 5, 10, 15 and 20 min. (a) Explain why ln C against t is a straight line. (b) Use the first and last readings to find the half-life, in minutes.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '10', 'min', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) C = C₀e^(−λt) gives ln C = ln C₀ − λt. (b) λ = (ln 640 − ln 160) ÷ 20 = 0.06931 min⁻¹; t½ = ln 2 ÷ 0.06931 = 10.0 min. Mark scheme (5 marks). B1: linear form. C1: gradient = −λ. M1: t½ = ln 2/λ. C1: value. A1: t½ = 10 min.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 438" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg740715c8-t fg740715c8-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg740715c8-t">Count rate against time</title><desc id="fg740715c8-d">Table and graph of corrected count rate against time: 640, 452, 320, 226 and 160 counts per minute at 0, 5, 10, 15 and 20 min, a falling curve.</desc><g transform="translate(0,0)"><rect x="76" y="8" width="247.9" height="168" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="76" y="8" width="247.9" height="28" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="112" y="22" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">t / min</text><text x="236" y="22" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">C / counts per minute</text><line x1="148.1" y1="8" x2="148.1" y2="176" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:r