('8aa19126-7de4-51be-bb27-fb1fd511b5d3', '50ff4bc9-26e6-445a-abf4-2137ff76c6eb', 'ce473f5f-8864-4efe-be59-be54ed9c0caa', 'a-level', 'P2.3', '9702 coursebook P2.3 · Analysis of the data', 49, 49, 'For a black body, P = kTⁿ is expected with n = 4. A graph of lg P against lg T passes through (3.20, 1.30) and (3.50, 2.47). (a) Calculate the gradient. (b) Calculate the percentage difference between this gradient and 4.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.5', '%', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) Gradient = (2.47 − 1.30) ÷ (3.50 − 3.20) = 3.9. (b) % difference = (4 − 3.9) ÷ 4 × 100 = 2.5 %. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: Δ(lg P). C1: gradient. M1: % difference. C1: value. A1: % difference = 2.50%.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg5b8c4c7a-t fg5b8c4c7a-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg5b8c4c7a-t">lg P against lg T</title><desc id="fg5b8c4c7a-d">A straight line on a graph of lg P against lg T through (3.20, 1.30) and (3.50, 2.47).</desc><line x1="33" y1="34" x2="33" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="102.8" y1="34" x2="102.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="172.6" y1="34" x2="172.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="242.4" y1="34" x2="242.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="312.2" y1="34" x2="312.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke