points lie on a straight line through the origin at first, then curve over at the highest loads.'),
('4f83d44e-3a10-57ba-b699-3dd74eb03520', '50ff4bc9-26e6-445a-abf4-2137ff76c6eb', '8b8b53aa-cac1-4dda-a21f-0e8b114d6d31', 'a-level', 'P2.5', '9702 coursebook P2.5 · Conclusions and evaluation of results', 51, 51, 'A glass block has refractive index n = 1.52 ± 0.03. (a) Calculate the speed of light in the glass. (b) Calculate the absolute uncertainty in this speed, in units of 10⁸ m s⁻¹. Take c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.03895', '10⁸ m s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) v = 3.00 × 10⁸ ÷ 1.52 = 1.974 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹. (b) % = 0.03 ÷ 1.52 × 100 = 1.97 %; Δv = 1.97 ÷ 100 × 1.974 × 10⁸ = 3.9 × 10⁶ m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: v = c/n. C1: % in n. M1: same % in v. C1: absolute. A1: Δv = 0.039 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('e9a94fb3-1911-5c89-a742-80ee7e2b38fe', '50ff4bc9-26e6-445a-abf4-2137ff76c6eb', '8b8b53aa-cac1-4dda-a21f-0e8b114d6d31', 'a-level', 'P2.5', '9702 coursebook P2.5 · Conclusions and evaluation of results', 52, 52, 'Five measurements of g are 9.62, 9.85, 9.74, 9.90 and 9.69 m s⁻². (a) Calculate the mean. (b) Estimate the uncertainty as half the range. (c) Calculate the percentage uncertainty.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.434', '%', false, 0.05, false, NULL, '(a) Mean = (9.62 + 9.85 + 9.74 + 9.90 + 9.69) ÷ 5 = 9.76 m s⁻². (b) Δg = (9.90 − 9.62) ÷ 2 = 0.14 m s⁻². (c) % = 0.14 ÷ 9.76 × 100 = 1.4 %. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: mean. C1: range. C1: half range. M1: % = Δg/g × 100. C1: value. A1: % uncertainty = 1.4%.', 6, NULL, NULL)
